## Could not date

**p183 Neal O'Mara / HelloSign.** Private company. Dropbox bought JN Projects in 2019 ($177.9M in the 10-K; $230M in the press). That is an acquisition price, and **acq50 is barred** because some revenue was published. Latka’s “$7.2M in 2016” sits **under** the 2016 bar of $7,454,953 (~3% short) and is not a filing. No 2017–18 annual figure at or above the bar. Guessing a year here would be the expensive error.

## Where I was uncertain

1. **Olsen 1958–1962.** First-year $94k (1958) and $6.535M (1962) are solid. I could not source 1959–61. Britannica’s “$1.3 million in 1960” did not load; even if true it would sit inside the range. FundingUniverse’s “$900k in 1964” contradicts DEC’s own $10.9M FY1964 and was ignored.

2. **Facebook 2004–2007.** The S-1 selected table begins at 2007 ($153M). TechCrunch said the S-1 had $382k / $9M / $48M for 2004–06; those sentences are **not** in the S-1 I fetched, so they were not used. If someone dated 2005 from TechCrunch, that is a citation error.

3. **Gil 2020.** The Form D that names Cosmic–Aleph 1 also names Cosmic–Bet 1; the $300M is the notice total. I still dated 2020 because Aleph 1 is an issuer on a first-sale notice that sold $300M against an $80.4M bar, and later Aleph funds are $620M / $1.1B. If the $300M were split equally, $150M is still 1.87× the bar — that split is **not sourced**. This is the row I would most want a second look at.

4. **Stephens 2023–2025.** April 2023 Form D: $0 sold, first sale yet to occur, Trae Stephens on the GP. October 2025 amendment: first sale 2023-04-07, $971.6M sold, Principals Fund on the same notice. Axios in December 2024 said Fund IX had not yet begun investing. I did not collapse this to 2023.

5. **ByteDance 2012–2020.** Eight years, still under the 10-year cap. Forbes 2017’s “>6 billion yuan / $869M in 2016” is an 86 Research estimate, not a company year, so it was not used to name 2016. CNBC’s $34.3B for 2020 is from an internal management meeting, which is the first USD figure I would actually defend.

6. **FedEx 1973–1975.** 1975 $43.5M is from the International Directory of Company Histories, not a 10-K. 1973/74 annual sales were not found. The 1975 figure is so far above the bar that the crossing is in 1973, 1974, or 1975.

7. **Apple FY vs calendar.** Apple’s year is the fiscal year ended late September. FY1978 is the first sourced year above the bar. I did not annualize the 1977 stub.

## Margins under 20% above the bar

None of the dated rows. HelloSign’s unverified 2016 $7.2M is **below** the bar, which is why that row is `unknown` rather than 2016.

Witten is a prize year, not a revenue test.

Rows were appended as each person was finished, not all at the end.
